{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1558006-how-is-sorcery-sustainable","id":1558006,"title":"How is Sorcery Sustainable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-29T20:14:50-08:00","id":1558006,"title":"How is Sorcery Sustainable?","content":"Okay, I know the whole premise of Curseborne is that you are, well, cursed. But when it comes to Sorcery, the effects of that curse seem way too extreme.<br /> <br /> From what I've been able to glean from people talking about the game, sorcery is powered by sacrificing something that's important to you. But it's more than just a professional hobby, it's a physical addiction. You NEED to perform magic on a nearly constant basis. Going more than a couple days without it causes you to start bleeding from every orifice, or some other manner of gruesome withdrawal symptoms.<br /> <br /> So that has me wondering just how exactly you're supposed to maintain a steady supply of sacrifices just to keep yourself alive? I mean, once you start running low on options, you'd be desperately trying to seize anything that falls in line with your family's preferred style, just to immediately destroy it. At that point, it stops being a 'sacrifice' and just becomes casting reagents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T11:06:22-08:00","id":1558025,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that's sort of the point. Being a Sorcerer is being a high-functioning addict. Your goal is to limit your casting of magic and need for sacrifices enough that you can acquire new sacrifices at a fast enough pace to sustain yourself. If you can't you'll start to spiral and eventually reach the point where you've sacrificed everything (I forgot what you turned into at that point, but it's bad). That's the horror, that if you can't manage it you become the equivalent of a junky willing to stab someone to death just for another hit, except you've got magic at the tips of your fingers.<br /> <br /> That said, IIRC the amount you need to sacrifice to maintain your normal level of magic isn't actually that bad, especially with your Family to help provide support and sacrifices in return for favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}